  "scope": [
    "Synthetic histories; no user recordings or production requests.",
    "Timings are medians after one warm-up, allocation instrumentation disabled.",
    "Startup compares only history-access work: before 1+3*N full cached copies; after folder metadata and one indexed body read per recording, reused for its three files. Neither includes common hashing, filesystem reconciliation, UI rendering or Tauri startup.",
    "Title update reads and durably saves one changed title. Baseline fsyncs the JSON file and parent; SQLite uses WAL and synchronous=FULL.",
    "History response compares the old full-history DTO with the new first page, including previews and counts. Later pages and full transcript expansion are separate on-demand operations.",
    "One-time import is reported separately; the JSON backup is retained unchanged.",
    "Allocation figures are cumulative Rust allocator requests, including reallocations; they exclude SQLite C allocations and are not peak RAM.",
    "Search timing uses a term matching all bodies and returns the first 50 matches; this is not a worst-case no-match search.",
    "No network latency, Swift capture or JavaScript rendering was measured.",
    "This is a live list with stable timestamp/ID ordering and offset pagination. Mutations between page requests can shift offsets; recording updates trigger a reload of the loaded range, duplicate IDs are removed and obsolete request generations are discarded. It is not a multi-page database snapshot."
  ],
